<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A9201005" svcinfotypenbr = "03" svcinfoqualnbr = "01" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
DRL System Description
</title>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
DRL system consists of BCM, lighting switch, ECM and DRLs.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
LED DRL works as DRL and clearance light as well.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0A920001.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "45.425mm" ver = "01" gw = "156" gh = "112"/>
</figure>
</item>
</list1>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A9201005001">
<title>
Operation
</title>
<ptxt>
When the lighting switch is OFF or in “CLEARANCE” position and front fog light switch is OFF while the engine is running or stationary by engine auto stop control, BCM (1) outputs DRL control signal to LED driver (4) and turns on LED DRL (3) as DRL. However, when the headlight or front fog light is ON, BCM turns off DRL and darken LED DRL for clearance light.
</ptxt>
